{
  "decision": "NO_CHANGE",
  "workflow_yaml": null,
  "rationale": "The workflow already applies the relevant evidence-supported dependency-cache optimization: the large pinned IntelliJ IDEA download is restored and saved with actions/cache using a version-pinned key (idea-${IDEA_VERSION}-linux), including a separate save step so the IDE is cached even when the style check fails. The JDK is provisioned by actions/setup-java from GitHub's tool cache. P-LIT-GHA-CACHE (cache dependency downloads) is not additionally applicable because its precondition requires a lockfile or environment input to key the cache, and this workflow runs a single-file Java program with no build tool or lockfile (no maven needed), so there is no dependency manifest to hash and no safe extra cache to add without disturbing the existing pinned IntelliJ cache. P-LIT-CUSTOM-TIMEOUT is not applied because cold-cache IntelliJ downloads are valid slow runs that could exceed a proposed limit (documented contraindication), and its benefit is simulation-estimated rather than measured for this workflow. There is no matrix to fail-fast, no build selection to gate, and no unused outputs to remove, so no change preserves coverage better than the current file.",
  "evidence_ids": ["P-LIT-GHA-CACHE", "P-LIT-CUSTOM-TIMEOUT"]
}
